{"id":1375,"date":"2026-02-18T22:15:43","date_gmt":"2026-02-18T22:15:43","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/aca2026kosovo.net\/?post_type=sessions&#038;p=1375"},"modified":"2026-05-30T10:05:39","modified_gmt":"2026-05-30T10:05:39","slug":"coding-theory-and-its-applications","status":"publish","type":"sessions","link":"https:\/\/aca2026kosovo.net\/sessions\/coding-theory-and-its-applications\/","title":{"rendered":"Coding Theory and Its Applications"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Abstract:<br>This special session focuses on current directions in coding theory<br>and its applications, bringing together algebraic, combinatorial,<br>and computational perspectives. Topics include structured code<br>families such as algebraic geometry codes, rank-metric codes,<br>additive codes, and codes with rich automorphism groups, as well<br>as parameter determination and bounds (including<br>Delsarte\/Levenshtein-type approaches and linear programming).<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">For ACA 2026, the session also considers themes related to quantum<br>error-correcting codes and their applications, including<br>connections with design theory (e.g., combinatorial designs<br>arising from code structures, incidence structures, and symmetry).<br>It also considers the covering radius and its generalizations,<br>exact and computational results for special families, and related<br>optimization and bounding techniques.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The session aims to foster interaction among researchers working<br>on theoretical developments, computational evidence, and<br>application-driven problems in classical and quantum coding theory.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"featured_media":0,"template":"","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"site-sidebar-layout":"default","site-content-layout":"","ast-site-content-layout":"default","site-content-style":"default","site-sidebar-style":"default","ast-global-header-display":"","ast-banner-title-visibility":"